#question(title: [Definition of maximum], centered: true)[
  Let $f$ be a function with domain $I$.  \
  Which one (or ones) of the following is (or
  are) a definition of #h(1em) “$f$ has a
  maximum on $I$"?

  + $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(exists C in RR)$ s.t.
    $display(f(x) <= C)$
  + $display(exists C in I)$ s.t.
    $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(f(x) <= C)$
  + $display(exists C in RR)$ s.t.
    $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(f(x) <= C)$
  + $display(exists C in RR)$ s.t.
    $display(forall x in I)$,
    $display(f(x) < C)$
]
